This written in a format suitable for IT governance, security architecture, audit documentation, and operational standards.
It aligns with NIST SP 800-207 (Zero Trust), Microsoft Zero Trust, CIS Benchmarks, and ISO 27001 governance principles.

Purpose:
Following by best practices, to ensure Azure Virtual Machines operate within a hardened, monitored, identity-driven, and segmented environment that aligns with Zero Trust principles and organizational governance requirements.

1. Establish Governance Foundation (Define the Boundary Model)
Methodology
 1.1 Define the VM as a security boundary
	* Hypervisor boundary
	* Guest OS boundary
	* Identity boundary
	* Network boundary
	* Data boundary

 1.2 Document the shared responsibility model
	* Azure protects the hypervisor and physical infrastructure.
	* The organization protects Identity, OS, Network, and Data.

 1.3 Adopt Zero Trust as the architectural baseline
	* Never trust, always verify
	* Assume breach
	* Enforce least privilege

Best Practices
Maintain a governance document describing VM boundaries
Ensure all teams understand that subnet are not security boundaries.
Require segmentation through NSGs, firewalls, and routing.

Validation action:
Review VM architecture diagrams quarterly
Confirm boundaries are documented in the IT governance library.
_______________________________________________________________________________

2. Identity Governance (Primary Zero Trust Control)

Methodology
 2.1 Enforce strong identity governance for VM access.
 2.2 Replace local accounts with Entra ID authentication.
 2.3 Use Privileged Identity Management (PIM) authentication.
 2.4 Require Just-In-Time access for SSH/ RDP.
 2.5 Apply least privilege RBAC at VM, disk, and resource group levels.

Best Practices
No standing admin access
No shared accounts.
No unmanaged SSH keys.
Managed Identity for all workloads.
Conditional Access for VM sign-in.

Validation actions:
Disable local admin accounts.
Require Entra ID login for Windows/ Linux
Enforce MFA and Conditional Access.
	Validation Commands:
	- PowerShell
	- Get-AzRoleAssignment -Scope (Get-AzVM -ResourceGroupName <RG> -Name <VM>).Id

	- Azure CLI (Bash)
	- az role assignment list --scope $(az vm show -g <RG> -n <VM --query id -o tsv)
Replace Local Accounts
	How to perform
	- Audit VM OS for local Accounts.
	- Remove or disable non-managed accounts.
	Validation commands (Windows):
	- PowerShell
	- Get-LocalUser

	- Bash (Linux):
	- cat /etc/passwd
Enforce PIM
	How to perform
	- Require elevation through Entra PIM for VM operators.
	- Remove permanent admin roles
	Validation action:
	- Review PIM assignments monthly
_______________________________________________________________________________

3. Network Segmentation & Boundary Enforcement

Methodology
 3.1 Treat the network as untrusted.
 3.2 Enforce segmentation using:
	NSGs
	Azure Firewall / NVA
	Custom Routes (UDRs)
	Virtual Network Manager (AVNM) Security Admin Rules
 3.3 Validate east-west traffic paths.
 3.4 Log and analyze all flows.

Best Practices
Deny-by-default NSG posture.
No direct subnet-to-subnet trust.
Route sensitive workloads through firewalls.
Use AVNM for global segmentation policies
Enable NSG Flow Logs + Traffic Analytics.
_______________________________________________________________________________

4. OS Hardening & Configuration Governance

Methodology
 4.1 Apply CIS or organizational baselines
 4.2 Enforce patching and configuration compliance.
 4.3 Control VM extensions and agents.
 4.4 Validate OS integrity and secure boot.

Best Practices
Disable unused services.
Enforce secure boot and vTPM.
Use Azure Update Manager for patch governance.
Audit VM extensions regularly.
______________________________________________________________________________

5. Data Protection & Encryption Governance

Methodology
 5.1 Enforce encryption at rest:
	* SSE with PMK
	* ADE or Confidential Disk Encryption
 5.2 Protect data in transit:
	* TLS enforcement
	* Private endpoints
 5.3 Control access to disks and snapshots

Best Practices
No unencrypted disks.
No public endpoints for storage.
RBAC restrictions on snapshot creation.
Use confidential computing for sensitive workloads.
_______________________________________________________________________________

6. Monitoring, Logging & Threat Detection Governance

Methodology
 6.1 Enable full telemetry:
	* Azure Monitor Agent
	* VM Insights
	* NSG Flow Logs
	* Activity Logs
	* Azure Firewall logs
 6.2 Integrate with SIEM (Microsoft Sentinel).
 6.3 Define alerting thresholds and escalation paths.

Best Practices
Log everything that touches the VM boundary.
Use Sentinel analytics for lateral movement detection.
Monitor identity anomalies (PIM, JIT, failed logins).
Enforce log retention aligned with compliance.
_______________________________________________________________________________

7. Compliance, Lifecycle & Operational Governance

Methodology
 7.1 Define VM lifecycle stages:
	* Request
	* Provision
	* Harden
	* Operate
	* Monitor
	* Decommission
 7.2 Enforce governance gates at each stage.
 7.3 Require periodic boundary validation.

Best Practices:
Quarterly VM boundary audits.
Automated compliance checks (Azure Policy).
Decommission VMs securely (wipe disk, revoke identities).
Maintain architecture diagrams and boundary documentation.
_______________________________________________________________________________

Example: governance validation script (PowerShell skeleton)
# Connect
´´´text
Connect-AzAccount
´´´

# 1. Get all VMs
´´´text
$vms = Get-AzVM
´´´

# 2. For each VM, validate key controls
´´´text
$report = foreach ($vm in $vms) {
    $nics = Get-AzNetworkInterface -ResourceGroupName $vm.ResourceGroupName |
            Where-Object { $_.VirtualMachine.Id -eq $vm.Id }

    $disks = Get-AzDisk -ResourceGroupName $vm.ResourceGroupName |
             Where-Object { $_.ManagedBy -eq $vm.Id }

    [PSCustomObject]@{
        VMName            = $vm.Name
        ResourceGroup     = $vm.ResourceGroupName
        HasNSG            = ($nics.NetworkSecurityGroup -ne $null)
        HasManagedIdentity= ($vm.Identity -ne $null)
        IsEncrypted       = ($disks.Encryption.Type -ne $null)
        HasPublicIP       = ($nics.IpConfigurations.PublicIpAddress -ne $null)
    }
}
´´´

# 3. Export quarterly report
´´´text
$timestamp = Get-Date -Format "yyyyMMdd"
$report | Export-Csv -Path "vm-governance-report-$timestamp.csv" -NoTypeInformation
´´´
_______________________________________________________________________________

Example: Azure Policy + alerts as code
Use ARM/Bicep/Terraform or PowerShell to:

Assign policies (e.g., “Require NSG on NIC”, “Require disk encryption”, “Deny public IP on VMs”).

Create Azure Monitor alerts via ARM templates or az monitor metrics/diagnostic-settings/alert commands.
______________________________________________________________________________

Conditional Access via script (high-level)
Use Entra ID PowerShell / Graph API to:

Create Conditional Access policies targeting:
VM sign-in (Azure AD sign-in to Azure resources).
Specific roles/groups (e.g., “VM Operators”).
Enforce MFA, compliant device, trusted locations.
_______________________________________________________________________________

Policy and alerts as code
Bicep – require NSG on NIC and disk encryption, plus a basic alert
´´´text
@description('Log Analytics workspace ID')
param logAnalyticsWorkspaceId string

@description('Scope for policy assignment')
param scope string

// Policy: Require NSG on NIC
resource policyRequireNsg 'Microsoft.Authorization/policyDefinitions@2023-03-01' = {
  name: 'require-nsg-on-nic'
  properties: {
    policyType: 'Custom'
    mode: 'Indexed'
    displayName: 'Require NSG on NIC'
    description: 'Ensures all NICs have an NSG associated.'
    policyRule: {
      if: {
        field: 'type'
        equals: 'Microsoft.Network/networkInterfaces'
      }
      then: {
        effect: 'auditIfNotExists'
        details: {
          type: 'Microsoft.Network/networkSecurityGroups'
          existenceCondition: {
            field: 'Microsoft.Network/networkInterfaces/networkSecurityGroup.id'
            notEquals: ''
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

resource assignRequireNsg 'Microsoft.Authorization/policyAssignments@2023-03-01' = {
  name: 'assign-require-nsg-on-nic'
  properties: {
    displayName: 'Require NSG on NIC'
    policyDefinitionId: policyRequireNsg.id
    scope: scope
  }
}

// Policy: Require disk encryption
resource policyRequireDiskEnc 'Microsoft.Authorization/policyDefinitions@2023-03-01' = {
  name: 'require-disk-encryption'
  properties: {
    policyType: 'Custom'
    mode: 'Indexed'
    displayName: 'Require disk encryption on managed disks'
    description: 'Ensures all managed disks are encrypted.'
    policyRule: {
      if: {
        field: 'type'
        equals: 'Microsoft.Compute/disks'
      }
      then: {
        effect: 'audit'
        details: {
          field: 'Microsoft.Compute/disks/encryption.type'
          equals: 'EncryptionAtRestWithPlatformKey'
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

resource assignRequireDiskEnc 'Microsoft.Authorization/policyAssignments@2023-03-01' = {
  name: 'assign-require-disk-encryption'
  properties: {
    displayName: 'Require disk encryption'
    policyDefinitionId: policyRequireDiskEnc.id
    scope: scope
  }
}

// Alert: VM with public IP (metric-based example)
resource actionGroup 'Microsoft.Insights/actionGroups@2022-06-01' = {
  name: 'vm-governance-actiongroup'
  location: 'global'
  properties: {
    groupShortName: 'vmgov'
    enabled: true
    emailReceivers: [
      {
        name: 'SecOpsEmail'
        emailAddress: 'secops@contoso.com'
        status: 'Enabled'
      }
    ]
  }
}

resource alertPublicIp 'Microsoft.Insights/metricAlerts@2023-01-01' = {
  name: 'vm-public-ip-alert'
  location: 'global'
  properties: {
    description: 'Alert when VMs with public IP are detected.'
    severity: 2
    enabled: true
    scopes: [
      scope
    ]
    evaluationFrequency: 'PT5M'
    windowSize: 'PT15M'
    criteria: {
      allOf: [
        {
          name: 'PublicIPCount'
          metricName: 'PublicIPCount'
          metricNamespace: 'custom/vmGovernance'
          operator: 'GreaterThan'
          threshold: 0
          timeAggregation: 'Average'
        }
      ]
    }
    actions: [
      {
        actionGroupId: actionGroup.id
      }
    ]
  }
}
´´´
_______________________________________________________________________________

Terraform – policy assignment and alert skeleton
´´´text
provider "azurerm" {
  features {}
}

variable "scope" {
  type = string
}

resource "azurerm_policy_definition" "require_nsg_on_nic" {
  name         = "require-nsg-on-nic"
  policy_type  = "Custom"
  mode         = "Indexed"
  display_name = "Require NSG on NIC"
  description  = "Ensures all NICs have an NSG associated."

  policy_rule = <<POLICY
{
  "if": {
    "field": "type",
    "equals": "Microsoft.Network/networkInterfaces"
  },
  "then": {
    "effect": "auditIfNotExists",
    "details": {
      "type": "Microsoft.Network/networkSecurityGroups",
      "existenceCondition": {
        "field": "Microsoft.Network/networkInterfaces/networkSecurityGroup.id",
        "notEquals": ""
      }
    }
  }
}
POLICY
}

resource "azurerm_policy_assignment" "assign_require_nsg_on_nic" {
  name                 = "assign-require-nsg-on-nic"
  display_name         = "Require NSG on NIC"
  policy_definition_id = azurerm_policy_definition.require_nsg_on_nic.id
  scope                = var.scope
}

resource "azurerm_monitor_action_group" "vm_governance" {
  name                = "vm-governance-actiongroup"
  resource_group_name = "rg-monitoring"
  short_name          = "vmgov"

  email_receiver {
    name          = "SecOpsEmail"
    email_address = "secops@contoso.com"
  }
}

resource "azurerm_monitor_metric_alert" "vm_public_ip_alert" {
  name                = "vm-public-ip-alert"
  resource_group_name = "rg-monitoring"
  scopes              = [var.scope]
  description         = "Alert when VMs with public IP are detected."
  severity            = 2
  enabled             = true
  frequency           = "PT5M"
  window_size         = "PT15M"

  criteria {
    metric_namespace = "custom/vmGovernance"
    metric_name      = "PublicIPCount"
    aggregation      = "Average"
    operator         = "GreaterThan"
    threshold        = 0
  }

  action {
    action_group_id = azurerm_monitor_action_group.vm_governance.id
  }
}
´´´
